encyclopedia :root_deck_symbiotes do
  name "The Graft"
  summary "The Graft joins engineered heat-movers, waste-eaters, and pulse-carriers through one graft-web chemistry. Garden habs exchange all three families together to maintain compatible root decks."
  kind :lifeform
  subkind :ecological_group
  status :complete
  log "2026-08-31 — Renamed The Consortium to The Graft; the title names the shared graft-web chemistry."
  topics :ecology, :trade, :"ring-hab", :"ring-era"
  prevalence :uncommon
  appears_when all: { place: [:garden] }
  origin "Bred for the ring's continuous root deck — the shared growing stratum that ran the habitats' whole length; every postfall line descends from stock isolated in the fragments"
  biology "Three interdependent families sharing one graft-web chemistry: heat-movers that pump warmth along root channels, waste-eaters that close nutrient loops, and pulse-carriers that pass warning signals between grafted beds"
  function "Living infrastructure: a stocked root deck heats itself evenly, cleans its own loops, and passes bed-to-bed warnings — and exchanging stock between habs keeps every line vigorous and every deck compatible"
  resonance_relation "The pulse-carriers signal in the structural band's lowest reaches, and a stocked deck's murmur is part of what gardeners mean by a hab sounding healthy"

  descriptive_identity(
    appearance: "Fine pale traceries follow roots and graft joins through a " \
                "stocked bed. Heat-movers, waste-eaters, and pulse-carriers " \
                "travel together in moss-packed jars labeled by source line.",
    behavior: "Each family works its layer of the shared web — heat pumped along " \
              "the root channels, waste drawn to the eaters' beds, pulses " \
              "passed graft to graft — and all three propagate along any " \
              "grafted join, which is why a gift of cuttings is also a gift of " \
              "everything living in them.",
    threat: "A line introduced without a test graft can overrun or reject local " \
            "channels. Cooperatives join samples under glass before opening " \
            "exchange stock to a deck.",
    senses: "Pulse-carriers respond to changes in graft-web chemistry and pass " \
            "a low structural-band murmur into neighboring beds.",
    risks: "Lines inbreed in isolation and drift apart. A deck stocked from " \
           "one source weakens over a generation, while incompatible lines " \
           "fail to form shared channels in a test graft."
  )

  prose <<~PROSE
    The elven ring's growing stratum was one continuous root deck. Its symbiotes were engineered as three interdependent families with one graft-web chemistry. Heat-movers pump warmth through root channels. Waste-eaters break down residues and return nutrients to the bed. Pulse-carriers respond to chemical stress and pass a low structural-band signal through connected grafts. The families propagate along the same joins and are exchanged together; a cutting from a stocked deck carries part of the Graft with it.

    The Glassfall isolated root-deck lines in separate habs. Lines maintained from one source lose vigor and can drift away from the chemistry of another deck. The graft trade therefore moves mixed stock between habs in moss-packed carrying jars. Cooperatives keep source pedigrees, join samples under glass, and introduce compatible stock gradually through a test bed.

    In a balanced deck, heat reaches cold corners, waste loops clear, pale channels remain continuous across grafts, and the pulse-carrier murmur passes bed to bed. Gardeners inspect those effects separately because one family can weaken before the others. Stock travels as gifts, traded lots, and reciprocal exchanges. Lines retain the names of the habs that kept them, and carrying jars are returned for reuse. The trade phrase *one deck, carried in jars* refers to compatibility maintained across fragments, not to a single organism or uniform strain.
  PROSE

  cue "The visiting gardener kneels at the deck's far corner, lays a palm flat where the heating plan says cold, and finds it warm — the heat-movers' work — and nods the professional nod that starts the stock negotiation."
  cue "At the season fair the carrying jars stand in labeled rows, moss-packed, pedigreed by hab and line, and two cooperatives' elders watch a graft join under glass to see whether their webs still know each other."
  affordance "A balanced Graft distributes heat, closes nutrient loops, and carries chemical-stress signals through connected beds. Exchanges maintain vigor and compatibility between isolated decks."
  variation "The three families balance differently by deck — cold-country habs run heavy heat-mover stock, dense urban gardens lean on the waste-eaters, and the big terrace systems prize pulse-carrier lines that reach across their whole stepped length."
  variation "Line pedigrees carry politics — old habs' stock trades on reputation, rising habs buy standing through generous gifting, and the cooperatives' pedigree books settle by record what the fair-ground arguments start."
end
